{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731254Z","id":"aa1344c28799fc184a41e2f18b50fc3751794d662961edb93a0ce5c4df9f3d0b","body":{"detail":"While a page's own scripts hold up the parse, comment mode and use() wait for it with no sign to the viewer. This needs a protocol addition: the bridge reports that it is waiting.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"21752b7263ca6b42a47eaef764ade6ba85f1d6e668c14f22c1a65849231a7eb0"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a wait for the parse, and the shell show a hint ('waiting for the page').","summary":"The shell shows nothing while the bridge waits for the page's parse","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:56:14.752276Z","id":"a4e0fc3d2449cef6e4c9e5c62dbf3e8fb48354924f9738b81f8f488f38ead924","body":{"detail":"The tests in web/bridge/test/long-press.test.ts and comment-mode.test.ts dispatch synthetic TouchEvents in jsdom. Three browser behaviours they cannot show: (1) that the cancelled touchend still grants the frame user activation, which the shell requires before it takes clax:pick-start (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 3.5); (2) that Android Chrome/WebView still delivers touchend, not touchcancel, after the long-press contextmenu that comment-mode.ts cancels; (3) that no click is synthesized after the cancelled touchend (comment-mode.ts swallows one within 800 ms in case it is).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":127},"content_hash":"571b41cf4f06dcc085a48acdbdbb6ab4e2f8e92aa64da6e4cecd98a8a433efd1"},"suggested_fix":"Exercise a long-press in the Playwright app-mode e2e with touch emulation (hasTouch) and on an Android device or emulator, and confirm a composer opens with a clip.","summary":"Long-press pick on a real Android WebView is unverified: activation, contextmenu and touchcancel","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/scroll.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:56:14.752447Z","id":"e941822a7ca1c95d030d297f6a807ef7f3fddb5f5be19dda259c85474a638073","body":{"detail":"While the document is too short to reach y, restoreScroll retries every 100 ms for up to 2000 ms and then scrolls to y. If the viewer scrolls the new version during that wait, the restore still moves the page under them once the document grows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"976d3a24272d77f4d4c99c457071ba7ccbbcea345f4836021a184237edf283ff"},"suggested_fix":"Stop the retries on a trusted wheel, touchmove or keydown in the page before the restore lands.","summary":"restoreScroll does not yield to the viewer's own scroll while it waits","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:56:14.752506Z","id":"e1b031787c5b47428ae04fd423d22b787be0f555daa0892ef65a8ee3a02a3c57","body":{"detail":"Measured with esbuild (minified, gzip -9) from the bridge source before and after commit 8a2ff314: eager bridge 5056 -> 5413 bytes, comment part 10766 -> 11644 bytes. Budgets are bridge 5501 and partComment 11821, recorded as measured size plus 10 percent, so both still fit, with under 200 bytes of headroom each. Not measured with scripts/bundle-size.mjs against a full npm run build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"015be019c0dd9e8ca33aafae42fbc53ff955e37b8a61197bc513fdb116f567da"},"summary":"The scroll report grows the eager bridge by about 360 bytes gzip, close to web/perf/bundle-budget.json","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540247Z","id":"55af0158d10110046e5f31d886791cdf5e452e3e49fa0e2110b498f76cf5b6d6","body":{"detail":"Failure: in comment mode with a mouse, a plain drag over text (no Shift, no Option) no longer selects text, so onUp finds a collapsed selection and the click that follows picks the enclosing element instead of a range. Option+drag selection widening likewise picks the wrong element. set(true) cancels selectstart (line 125) and setGuard adds GUARD_CSS (line 54: user-select:none on html) for every input type, not only touch. Reproduced: `CLAX_TEST_BIN=<debug clax> npx playwright test e2e/area.spec.ts -g 'plain text drag|drag selection made with Option'` fails 4/4 at commit 8a2ff314 ('Expected: range, Received: element' at area.spec.ts:179; '#panel' for '#para' at area.spec.ts:294). A bare Chromium page with the same style and selectstart listener confirms a mouse drag selects nothing. The jsdom tests in web/bridge/test/comment-mode.test.ts set selections programmatically and cannot see it. Right-click menus in comment mode are also cancelled on desktop now.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"159eeceaa541441fdc5b42a209f0f871671e4558de278914c95bc589a426ee79"},"suggested_fix":"Scope the guard to touch: cancel selectstart and contextmenu only while a LongPress hold is in progress (between touchstart and its end or abandon), or add the user-select style only for that span, and keep -webkit-touch-callout:none (which has no mouse effect). Re-run e2e/area.spec.ts.","summary":"The selection guard breaks mouse drag-select comments on desktop and in the extension overlay","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540469Z","id":"4858358cf08573e04b7597aff73fccdba719df2e55b82edce3bdf40e69ea1a3a","body":{"detail":"Failure: in the browser shell with touch (Playwright hasTouch/isMobile, 390x800, subdomain and sandbox), entering comment mode by the Comment button (tap or click), then a CDP Input.dispatchTouchEvent touchStart held 800 ms on an <h2> and touchEnd: the bridge outlines the target (one clax:hover) and posts clax:pick-start, navigator.userActivation.isActive is true in the shell, but document.activeElement in the shell is still the Comment BUTTON, so frameGesture() (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts, rule 2: focus in the content frame) refuses the start and no composer opens. A short tap on the same point opens the composer (control passes). The cancelled touchend suppresses the compatibility mousedown that would focus the frame, and touchPick does not call focusPage() as the area drag's press does (line 406). Activation itself is granted on the cancelled touchend.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":374},"end":{"line":381},"content_hash":"75cbd53400d882431e5fe2bf404faa3bbb216cd9245c54a96684b19db6182397"},"suggested_fix":"Call focusPage() in touchPick (or on arm) before pickAt, then confirm gesture.ts rule 3 counts the arrival for a touch hold (a mouseover may not be sent for a long-press); pin it with the long-press e2e in web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts, asserting the composer opens.","summary":"A long-press pick is refused by the shell: focus never enters the frame","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540556Z","id":"858abcf779a069ccf3859df10e5e4263cdd04a47aa2ed142453cde61afa3cfde","body":{"detail":"Measured with web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs on full `npm run build`s of git archives of 8a2ff314^ and 8a2ff314: eager bridge 5462 -> 5821 (+359; budget 5501), artifact entry 64006 -> 64008 (+2; budget 64006), comment part 10825 -> 11714 (+889; budget 11821, 107 left), extension overlay 17979 -> 18922. So scripts/quality_gates.sh's bundle lane fails until web/perf/bundle-budget.json is raised. The eager growth is reportScroll and the restore handler, which only the app shell (welcome app: true) uses.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":274},"end":{"line":274},"content_hash":"c369ab4b89d3932cfe40469d0c393fbb0ade276010f99c29b465d48bfe20a834"},"suggested_fix":"Load scroll.ts as a lazy bridge part on the app welcome so browsers outside the app pay nothing, or raise the bridge and artifact budgets by the measured growth in the same branch before the gates run.","summary":"bundle-size.mjs fails at 8a2ff314: eager bridge 5821 > 5501 and artifact 64008 > 64006","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540605Z","id":"99ab96e8c2f6a3fdd6757b08b5dff94b5485c79044c811ab6ad116be3bad23ef","body":{"detail":"LongPress.onEnd cancels the touchend (web/bridge/src/long-press.ts:125), so Chromium synthesizes no click after a long-press pick; the swallow window set in touchPick (line 379) then consumes the next genuine click within 800 ms instead, for example a quick tap after a refused pick. Nothing tests that no click arrives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":450},"end":{"line":455},"content_hash":"eaaddc1804a6d9296a16c6f4e183253b6d32303658c0017de1c7c36df32bd72d"},"suggested_fix":"Swallow only a click whose coordinates match the pick's release point within the slop, or drop the window if the e2e shows no click follows a cancelled touchend.","summary":"The 800 ms click swallow eats the viewer's next real tap or click","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/scroll.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540646Z","id":"a9fc8068284b1850905aa45b8b0431893d3961612ca271450e73fa3d6c6d52e7","body":{"detail":"When the newer version is shorter than y, restoreScroll retries for 2000 ms and gives up without scrolling, so the viewer lands at the top rather than as close to their place as the page allows.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"976d3a24272d77f4d4c99c457071ba7ccbbcea345f4836021a184237edf283ff"},"suggested_fix":"At the deadline, scroll to min(y, scrollHeight - innerHeight).","summary":"A restore past the new version's end leaves the page at the top","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540698Z","id":"aca9cb05d6ec3c2b88189e727ae0a2131330948841fad76d70e6c93c9521d769","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e1b031787c5b47428ae04fd423d22b787be0f555daa0892ef65a8ee3a02a3c57","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"015be019c0dd9e8ca33aafae42fbc53ff955e37b8a61197bc513fdb116f567da"},"summary":"Measured with scripts/bundle-size.mjs on full builds: both bridge and artifact are over budget, not under (eager bridge 5462 -> 5821 vs 5501; artifact 64006 -> 64008 vs 64006). See the concern on web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:274.","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.332445Z","id":"f67360bcacf735462dd6a8bcdcc68a4e8dac52fb162c73d11d095110d0005f3f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ef912931","summary":"Fixed in ef912931: selectstart and contextmenu are cancelled only while LongPress.holding (a finger down), and the guard style is only -webkit-touch-callout:none. Evidence: `CLAX_TEST_BIN=<stable debug clax> npx playwright test e2e/area.spec.ts -g 'plain text drag|drag selection made with Option'` after a fresh npm run build: 4 passed. Regression test web/bridge/test/comment-mode.test.ts 'mouse_selection_and_context_menu_are_untouched' passes (fails against 8a2ff314).","supersedes":"55af0158d10110046e5f31d886791cdf5e452e3e49fa0e2110b498f76cf5b6d6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.332640Z","id":"f55949bbf18b712523b85e9bfd84627ae95ac680d2b6f2a2f160daba59d27287","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:41b86c25","summary":"Fixed in 41b86c25: the long-press no longer cancels touchend. In Chromium the release is then followed by the browser's compatibility mouse events and click, which deliver a trusted mouseover of iframe.frame to the shell (the counted arrival) and move focus into the frame; the click picks through onClick. With touchend cancelled the shell saw no pointer event at all during or after the hold (diagnosed with a capture listener on the shell window). When no click follows within TOUCH_CLICK_WAIT_MS, comment mode calls focusPage() and picks itself. Evidence: `npx playwright test e2e/long-press.spec.ts` (hasTouch, isMobile, 390x800, CDP touchStart held 800 ms then touchEnd, subdomain and sandbox): 4 passed, composer visible with its textarea focused; the same spec failed 4 of 4 at ef912931 (focusPage on a cancelled release). Wider run of area, bridge-comment, comment-targets, comment-flows, bridge-parts and long-press specs: 76 passed.","supersedes":"4858358cf08573e04b7597aff73fccdba719df2e55b82edce3bdf40e69ea1a3a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.332772Z","id":"27e1a93d63bbc4000ff20ff663f9404d98eac502a3d485e4621df5e8031105b1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:41b86c25","summary":"Fixed in 41b86c25 (the 800 ms swallow went in ef912931): no click is swallowed. The browser's click after a long-press release is the pick itself, and it clears the TOUCH_CLICK_WAIT_MS fallback timer. Evidence: web/bridge/test/comment-mode.test.ts 'the browser's click after a long-press picks, once' and 'leaves the viewer's next click after a long-press pick to pick again' pass.","supersedes":"99ab96e8c2f6a3fdd6757b08b5dff94b5485c79044c811ab6ad116be3bad23ef","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.332895Z","id":"e09532744172bf74f4ab0de7a0bf23b7c330af917da8a6e8bb0aedfcf511f5c1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:31fdb579","summary":"Fixed in 31fdb579: scroll.ts moved into the caps part, loaded on a welcome with app: true; the restore position rides on that welcome (restoreScroll), removing the clax:restore-scroll handler from the eager bridge; clax:scroll left out of BRIDGE_TYPES until the shell takes it. Evidence: npm run build plus node scripts/bundle-size.mjs on a copy of web/ at 41b86c25: 'gzip bytes: gallery 27771, artifact 64006, questions 14192, eager bridge 5492, parts: comment 11722, clip 15004, caps 8492, ...' with no budget exceeded (bridge 5501, artifact 64006, partComment 11821, partCaps 8773).","supersedes":"858abcf779a069ccf3859df10e5e4263cdd04a47aa2ed142453cde61afa3cfde","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/scroll.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.333012Z","id":"e64dd1c356a9cbc89de06fe5d3f8b343ac26403a04fa817c5d6beec164d63f92","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e1f1919d","summary":"Fixed in e1f1919d: at the 2000 ms deadline restoreScroll scrolls to min(y, scrollHeight - innerHeight), never below 0. Evidence: web/bridge/test/scroll.test.ts 'after 2000 ms in all, scrolls as far towards the position as the document reaches' and 'after 2000 ms, a document shorter than the viewport stays at the top' pass (both failed before the change).","supersedes":"a9fc8068284b1850905aa45b8b0431893d3961612ca271450e73fa3d6c6d52e7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.333127Z","id":"70cf300ec1bc09d73fc04226047ea222b2c3b28ee10ceb677a04986100ef4a74","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:31fdb579","summary":"The esbuild estimate here was wrong (see reply aca9cb05: the gate measured 5821). Superseded by the fix for 858abcf7 in 31fdb579: the eager bridge measures 5492 against 5501.","supersedes":"e1b031787c5b47428ae04fd423d22b787be0f555daa0892ef65a8ee3a02a3c57","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.333273Z","id":"8cc89df609baf79c6898d7d444ed713bf4c7a923c04b9d99a7417398c63ef2f2","body":{"detail":"web/e2e/long-press.spec.ts proves the pick in desktop Chromium with touch emulation, where a CDP hold of 800 ms released without a cancelled touchend is followed by mousemove, mousedown, mouseup and click (no contextmenu): the click picks, and its mouseover of iframe.frame and focus entry satisfy frameGesture() in web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts. On Android a real long-press raises GestureLongPress and contextmenu (cancelled while LongPress.holding) and may send no click after the release. Then comment-mode.ts touchPick picks after TOUCH_CLICK_WAIT_MS (400 ms) with focusPage(), and the shell takes it only if it counted the finger's arrival on the frame (rule 3), which nothing in the hold may provide: the pick would be refused. Also unverified: that touchend, not touchcancel, follows the cancelled contextmenu. The 400 ms wait is a guess at how late a click can come under load; a click later than that is blocked by the pick it raced (capturing).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"ae8608224a3fa6b35096501bd138682364ec9108ef497a680eb10d1fd2ac2115"},"suggested_fix":"Run the long-press on an Android device or emulator in the app (F8/F10). If the fallback pick is refused, the shell needs a touch arrival signal (for example a bridge-reported hold confirmed by the frame's activation), which is a change to gesture.ts's rules for the owner to decide.","summary":"Long-press on a real Android WebView is unverified: whether a click follows the release, and the no-click fallback's gesture","supersedes":"a4e0fc3d2449cef6e4c9e5c62dbf3e8fb48354924f9738b81f8f488f38ead924","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.333418Z","id":"d86448df32848684cf8d6ac6b9fc30e6d076dabd8a0d5b9981b255c10ca2c05e","body":{"detail":"The bridge posts clax:scroll after a welcome with app: true (web/bridge/src/scroll.ts), but BRIDGE_TYPES omits it, so web/shell/src/bridge-link.ts drops it. It was left out because the string alone moves the artifact bundle from 64006 to 64008 gzip bytes, over web/perf/bundle-budget.json's artifact budget of 64006, and no shell code reads the message yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"493ddf5c20216e677c89e3b913b63684f8c244e029795a0042014575bdf9841c"},"suggested_fix":"When the app shell (plan Task W2) reads clax:scroll, add it to BRIDGE_TYPES in the same change, with the artifact budget raised for the shell's app mode.","summary":"clax:scroll is not in BRIDGE_TYPES: the shell drops the scroll report until its app mode adds it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:20:28.379485Z","id":"2711ab9e277c70338403afa775453dd176bffd3671441c461bc856429ba47ff8","body":{"detail":"The shell answers each clax:hello with a welcome (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:1107), and the bridge re-sends hello on clax:greet (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:279). appScroll (web/bridge/src/scroll.ts) restores every position a welcome carries (web/bridge/test/scroll.test.ts 'restores each position it is given'), so if the app shell keeps restoreScroll on later welcomes for the same document, the page jumps back under a viewer who has scrolled since.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"a570438535dc062bc2028c3ed5f90eaad066d3aa351ed711f39efcc8bfc3ef40"},"suggested_fix":"In the shell's app mode, put restoreScroll only on the first welcome after loading a newer version, and pin that with a controller test; or have the bridge honour it once per document.","summary":"Every welcome carrying restoreScroll scrolls again, including a re-greet's","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152743Z","id":"6176f973aef931fd40856ffbf80471622736ad1398e05cab34546774dc7137b9","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts ctl.app.welcome consumes the pending restore on the first welcome; test web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'auto_follow_loads_a_newer_version_and_asks_the_bridge_to_restore_scroll' checks a re-greet's welcome has no restoreScroll.","kind":"comment","references":"2711ab9e277c70338403afa775453dd176bffd3671441c461bc856429ba47ff8","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"a570438535dc062bc2028c3ed5f90eaad066d3aa351ed711f39efcc8bfc3ef40"},"summary":"Done in bba79ce3: the app shell puts restoreScroll only on the first welcome after a newer version loads","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152786Z","id":"e0466ac9df3dc279087cfed11821e8b635043ac1ac342867eabd887ae5a3fbe6","body":{"detail":"Budget effect recorded on web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts:18.","kind":"comment","references":"d86448df32848684cf8d6ac6b9fc30e6d076dabd8a0d5b9981b255c10ca2c05e","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"17d581a29ca62aed0ab5f96cfbdfa748a66a60e2360f4b050e862a6b1ee2ebfd"},"summary":"Done in bba79ce3: clax:scroll is in BRIDGE_TYPES and read by web/shell/src/app/host.ts (onMessage)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152905Z","id":"196c5eb4376083830026e9b9948dcdfa4ad897cb916132de56e573da457b1f4b","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts hostArrival, web/shell/src/app/host.ts attestPointer; security reasoning in the waiver on host.ts:221:230. Still open: the Flutter side (plan Task F8) must call it on every pointer down and up its Listener sees over the WebView, in WebView CSS pixels, and a real Android run must confirm the pick is taken.","kind":"comment","references":"8cc89df609baf79c6898d7d444ed713bf4c7a923c04b9d99a7417398c63ef2f2","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"ae8608224a3fa6b35096501bd138682364ec9108ef497a680eb10d1fd2ac2115"},"summary":"Shell side of the no-click fallback built in bba79ce3: claxHost.attestPointer({x, y}) counts as the finger's arrival for 1 s in app mode","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
