{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:46:59.393843Z","id":"27b0edb18b5f915593491212487c96e5b6b833195ba318674e5cad21aaa6bce8","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart _attest and host_protocol.dart AttestPointer; covered by app_screen_test.dart 'every pointer down and up on the page is attested in page pixels'. A device run confirming the pick is taken is still needed (record on app_screen.dart:402:414).","kind":"comment","references":"8cc89df609baf79c6898d7d444ed713bf4c7a923c04b9d99a7417398c63ef2f2","summary":"Flutter side of the attestation built in 9825918c: every pointer down and up over the WebView calls claxHost.attestPointer({pointer, phase, x, y}) in the page's CSS pixels","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:01:06.200394Z","id":"a51ac6783dfdd861cbe8701afe5769ada6913086e37ab5a006f637c4245f096b","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs at d8e1224c: 'bridge: 5508 gzip bytes, over its budget of 5501' (5493 at 1405ba3b, measured from a clean archive of that commit). The growth is the desc key PickFlow.start posts and the part.desc(el) argument here; describe.ts itself is in the lazy comment part (11722 -> 11785, inside its 11821 budget). web/perf/bundle-budget.json is unchanged; Task W4 owns it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":176},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"731a435daaf3f9167f857c2cbe63f5ce5761f9f42b6d9bc212ece462aa9e5f29"},"suggested_fix":"Raise the bridge budget to 5565 (5501 + 15 rounded up to 64) in Task W4.","summary":"The eager bridge is 5508 gzip bytes, 7 over its 5501 budget, from the pick start's element description","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:19:10.698336Z","id":"84cc31df321f2ea6d6754f239524c0d2be03d97b8b99b9580ef491b86f62a13c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0bfa971b","summary":"Budget raised to 5565 in 0bfa971b. node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after a fresh scripts/build-web.sh: 'eager bridge 5508' with no budget exceeded, exit 0.","supersedes":"a51ac6783dfdd861cbe8701afe5769ada6913086e37ab5a006f637c4245f096b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:28:06.107592Z","id":"552b0eb0074586be23b5f3a8907ceabd3e76945f20f5791ac0939fb82b54f689","body":{"detail":"web/bridge/test/long-press.test.ts and comment-mode.test.ts ('hold, then drag') dispatch synthetic TouchEvents in jsdom, which always honour preventDefault. Three browser behaviours they cannot show: (1) that the touchmove crossing SLOP_PX after HOLD_MS is still cancelable on Android WebView and WKWebView, so the page does not scroll during the drag (Chrome ignores preventDefault on a touchmove it has already handed to scrolling, and sends touchcancel, which abandons the drag); (2) that the browser's long-press text selection (cancelled by comment-mode.ts onHeld on selectstart) does not instead grab the drag as a native selection handle drag; (3) that the selection made with Selection.setBaseAndExtent shows on a touch device with the ::selection tint set by CommentMode.setGuard (web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts:190).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":128},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"641474a8e7067be7f18a03348af3b7fe5da25f12fe15dbfa40a6d5c72ec4bd82"},"suggested_fix":"Exercise hold-drag in the Playwright e2e with touch emulation, and on an Android device and an iPhone/macOS WKWebView: hold 450 ms on text and drag, hold on an image and drag, and confirm no scroll, a tinted selection or a box, and a composer with the picked range or area.","summary":"Hold-then-drag on a real touch WebView is unverified: whether the move past the slop is still cancelable, and whether the browser's own long-press gesture takes the touch first","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:28:06.107670Z","id":"f502853533814809ab544dc972d67fa2cca7c8a3e2fae89b42f50c48096c3871","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8cc89df609baf79c6898d7d444ed713bf4c7a923c04b9d99a7417398c63ef2f2","summary":"A hold-then-drag release (comment-mode.ts touchDragEnd) picks on touchend with no click to follow, as this record's no-click fallback does: it calls window.focus() first and relies on the same touchend activation and, in app mode, the host's pointer attestation (record 8cc89df6) for the shell to take the pick.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:39:06.892124Z","id":"18c8929cf710c68a7aa31eda0f300410ff654ff65b4753ed244be6b01e014e01","body":{"detail":"installErrorRing runs for every framed page (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:103), not only the inspect view, which the bridge cannot know before its first script: devtools then attributes console.error calls to the bridge's wrapper, and the newest 20 calls' arguments stay referenced until they leave the ring (words are made only in errorsOf, in the clip part, to keep the eager bridge small). A page that replaces console.error without calling the function it replaced hides its later console errors from an inspection.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"04864742295da61691a5ba3a06124e59a08580af949fbcc95fc4d18572eb9812"},"summary":"The error ring wraps console.error on every framed page and keeps the logged values","tags":["inspect","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect-render.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:39:06.892203Z","id":"d82ce354e2cbe7b1c54e512a57351ba028214d51ebc5775af4150f2aea93a0a1","body":{"detail":"web/bridge/test/bridge-inspect.test.ts mocks it; the crop (the body translated by its client box so the viewport sits in a w x h picture) and the opaque-origin sandbox path are unverified in a browser until the Playwright inspect spec (web/e2e/inspect.spec.ts) checks that ?inspect=1 returns a PNG of what the viewport shows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"09b9c9545b3a9c2ec3463fe9815eb9d8388bed37f56171e9aa83eb7805485959"},"summary":"renderViewport has run only as a stub under jsdom","tags":["inspect","test-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:40:55.697663Z","id":"372b576877940ee25fc4479c97557dedc8140a569ed423939d8fb507d1d98a06","body":{"detail":"Failure: Chromium with hasTouch/isMobile (390x800), subdomain and sandbox modes, comment mode on via a tap on Comment; CDP Input.dispatchTouchEvent touchStart on #p (or on an <img>), held 800 ms, eight touchMoves 160 px right (or 120x100 down-right), touchEnd. The bridge builds the right anchor (range quote 'Grow revenue in ev', prefix/suffix set; area rect 120x100, area {x:0.3,y:0.25,w:0.4,h:0.5}), the page does not scroll and the selection is cleared, but clax:pick-start is answered clax:pick-refused and clax:pick arrives with clipError NOT_TAKEN. Cause: web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts checks frameGesture() synchronously on clax:pick-start, and its condition 3 (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts header) needs the pointer's arrival on iframe.frame counted by a shell mouseover or a click; a touch that moved after a long-press sends no compatibility mouse events and no click, so the window.focus() in touchDragEnd moves focus but no arrival counts. A hold-release without a drag works only because Chromium sends mousemove/mousedown/mouseup/click after it (web/e2e/long-press.spec.ts). Unit tests in web/bridge/test/comment-mode.test.ts call hooks directly, so they cannot see the shell's refusal. Shell window had userActivation.isActive true and document.activeElement iframe.frame after the release.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":466},"end":{"line":498},"content_hash":"42eb9478a492d51288b76133396113f43f493a60525e1889904c307c7bd7c3ad"},"suggested_fix":"Needs a shell-side arrival for a touch drag outside app mode, or a confirming tap: e.g. keep the dragged selection or box after release and pick on the next tap inside it (its click brings the counted arrival), or have the bridge pick on the browser's click when one comes and otherwise show the hint. Then a Playwright spec (web/e2e/hold-drag.spec.ts, Task W7) asserting the composer opens with the range quote and the area rect in both frame modes.","summary":"In a browser on touch, a hold-then-drag pick is refused by the shell: the composer never opens and the pick carries 'it was not taken'","tags":["review","touch","gesture","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:40:55.697794Z","id":"732f781051fb5d7ce74ea33a54f80a56f415c7584443ef65425b28cde40a9c4c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"552b0eb0074586be23b5f3a8907ceabd3e76945f20f5791ac0939fb82b54f689","summary":"Desktop Chromium touch emulation answers (1) and (2), not (3): after an 800 ms CDP hold, every touchmove was cancelable, preventDefault held the page at scrollY 0 through the drag, and no contextmenu, selectstart or touchcancel came; a 300 px swipe without the hold scrolled the page and posted no clax:pick-start. The ::selection tint was not checked, and a real Android WebView and WKWebView are still unverified. Separately, the pick these drags make is refused by the shell (blocker on web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts:466:498).","tags":["review","needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
